  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title level="a" type="main" coords="1,72.00,94.53,455.28,19.46">Revisiting Quadratic Attention on Modern Hardware</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <profileDesc>
        <abstract>
          <div>
            <p><s>We revisit the assumption that attention is the bottleneck.</s><s>Our measurements contradict the received view <ref type="bibr" target="#b1">[2]</ref>.</s></p>
          </div>
        </abstract>
      </profileDesc>
    </fileDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text xml:lang="en">
    <body>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
        <head n="1" coords="2,72.00,120.00,100.00,12.00">Introduction</head>
        <p coords="2,72.00,140.00,455.00,60.00"><s>Transformer models dominate sequence modelling <ref type="bibr" target="#b0">[1]</ref>.</s><s>A long line of efficiency work has followed <ref type="bibr" target="#b1">[2]</ref><ref type="bibr" target="#b2">[3]</ref>.</s><s>We disagree with the framing in <ref type="bibr" target="#b99">[42]</ref>.</s></p>
        <p><s>This paper makes three contributions.</s></p>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
        <head n="2.1">Experimental Setup</head>
        <p><s>We follow the standard recipe of <ref type="bibr" target="#b0">[1]</ref> without modification.</s></p>
        <formula xml:id="formula_0">A(Q, K, V ) = softmax(QK T )V</formula>
      </div>
      <figure xml:id="fig_0" coords="4,72.00,300.00,455.00,200.00">
        <head>Figure 1</head>
        <figDesc>Throughput against sequence length on an H100.</figDesc>
      </figure>
      <figure type="table" xml:id="tab_0">
        <head>Table 1</head>
